          "body": "## What the section can do that the document could not\n\nA section is a div. It is full width, it owns its layout entirely, and the reading measure\nlives inside the default section's own file rather than on the sheet — so a band that goes\nedge to edge costs nothing, and a column that wants 34rem of measure asks for it here.\n\n> Prose still wants a measure. A page that is edge to edge everywhere is exactly as\n> monotonous as one that is 34rem everywhere.\n\nThe freedom is to choose per section. Two columns where a figure earns its place beside the\nargument; one column where the words are the whole of it; a grid where things are being\ncompared. A page that chooses the same shape every time has not used any of it.\n\nSwap this slot's prose for the real argument, and swap `kpiName`, `kpiValue`, `barName` and\n`barValue` for the real figures. The tallest bar lights itself, so nothing here has to be\ntold which one matters.\n",
